.SH NAME
quotadial \- Track Claude, ChatGPT/Codex and Antigravity usage limits
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBquotadial\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Track Claude, ChatGPT/Codex and Antigravity usage limits.
.PP
QuotaDial shows how much of each Claude and ChatGPT/Codex plan limit is used, when each resets, and how old every number is. Claude\*(Aqs limits come from what Claude Code\*(Aqs status line hands `quotadial claude status\-line`, and its sign\-in is never read. It reads the sign\-in the Codex CLI already stores, and never writes it. A Gemini CLI account it finds signed in is listed too, with why it has no numbers, and its sign\-in is never opened. Antigravity\*(Aqs limits come from what Antigravity CLI\*(Aqs status line hands `quotadial antigravity status\-line`, and its sign\-in is never read. `qd` is the same command, shorter.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
quotadial\-status(1)
Show current usage for every account this machine is signed in to
.TP
quotadial\-watch(1)
Keep showing usage, refreshing every minute. No provider is asked more often than its own limit, so most refreshes show cached numbers with their age
.TP
quotadial\-daemon(1)
Run the daemon until Ctrl\-C: the one poller every consumer shares, with history and the local API. While it runs, `status` and `watch` ask it instead of polling
.TP
quotadial\-mcp(1)
Run the MCP server named quotadial on standard input and output, for agents such as Claude Code and Codex. Like `status`, it asks the daemon while one runs
.TP
quotadial\-alerts(1)
List the alert rules and what they told lately, or add, remove, or turn one on or off. Rules are written in plain words, such as `quotadial alerts add "warn me at 80%"`
.TP
quotadial\-doctor(1)
Print what support asks for, with nothing secret in it: the version, the system, the licence, the daemon, every account and where its sign\-in is, the problems and the settings. The app\*(Aqs Send feedback attaches the same
.TP
quotadial\-licence(1)
Say whether this copy is QuotaDial Free or QuotaDial Pro, or add or remove its licence key. A key is checked on this machine, with no network call
.TP
quotadial\-history(1)
Show how each window was used over time, from the daemon\*(Aqs history
.TP
quotadial\-claude(1)
Commands the Claude provider adds
.TP
quotadial\-antigravity(1)
Commands the Antigravity provider adds
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
quotadial status                        every account\*(Aqs windows now
quotadial status \-\-json                 the same, for a script or an agent
quotadial alerts add "warn me at 80%"   an alert rule in plain words
quotadial history \-\-since 30d \-\-csv     every reading of the last 30 days
quotadial licence add                   paste a QuotaDial Pro key
.fi
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
It worked. For status, every account produced a snapshot, whatever its status: check each snapshot\*(Aqs status.
.TP
\fB1\fR
Something failed: a provider or account produced no snapshot, a running daemon did not answer, or the output could not be written. What went wrong, and what to do, is on standard error.
.TP
\fB2\fR
The arguments were not understood.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBQUOTADIAL_DATA_DIR\fR
The folder QuotaDial keeps its history, settings, licence key and the local API\*(Aqs token in, in place of the system\*(Aqs own.
.TP
\fBCLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR\fR
The folder Claude Code keeps its settings and account in, in place of ~/.claude. quotadial claude status\-line keeps that folder\*(Aqs numbers in a file of its own, and QuotaDial also looks in every other Claude Code folder on the machine. Claude Code\*(Aqs sign\-in is never read.
.TP
\fBCODEX_HOME\fR
The folder the Codex CLI keeps auth.json in, in place of ~/.codex.
.TP
\fBGEMINI_CLI_HOME\fR
The folder Gemini CLI keeps its .gemini folder in, in place of the home folder. QuotaDial only checks that its sign\-in is there and reads one field of its settings.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/Library/Application Support/quotadial\fR
On macOS: the history (history.db), config.json, the licence key, daemon.json while the daemon runs, and the local API\*(Aqs token.
.TP
\fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/quotadial or ~/.local/share/quotadial\fR
The same, on Linux.
.TP
\fI%APPDATA%\\quotadial\fR
The same, on Windows.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
quotadial\-status(1), quotadial\-watch(1), quotadial\-daemon(1), quotadial\-mcp(1), quotadial\-alerts(1), quotadial\-doctor(1), quotadial\-licence(1), quotadial\-history(1), quotadial\-claude(1), quotadial\-antigravity(1). The full guide is docs/CLI.md in QuotaDial\*(Aqs repository, https://github.com/pghmatt/quotadial, and quotadial.com.
